  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "If $f(x)=\\int_{-1}^{x}|t|$ dt, then for any $x \\geq 0, f(x)$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "6FeFP",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}\\left(1-x^{2}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3knbO",
      "text": "$1-x^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "GcvMk",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}\\left(1+x^{2}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "HMrm6",
      "text": "$1+x^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, \r\n$\\begin{aligned} f(x) &=\\int_{-1}^{x} t\\left|d t=\\int_{-1}^{0}\\right| t\\left|d t+\\int_{0}^{x}\\right| t \\mid d t \\\\ &=-\\int_{-1}^{0} t d t+\\int_{0}^{x} t d t \\\\ &=\\left[-\\frac{t^{2}}{2}\\right]_{-1}^{0}+\\left[\\frac{t^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{x} \\\\ &=-\\frac{1}{2}\\left(0^{2}-(-1)^{2}\\right)+\\frac{1}{2}\\left(x^{2}-0^{2}\\right) \\\\ &=-\\frac{1}{2}(-1)+\\frac{1}{2}\\left(x^{2}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(1+x^{2}\\right) \\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
